efs-prop" data-target="ch2-refs-prop">Refs as a prop, and forwardRef</a></li><li><a href="#ch2-contract" data-target="ch2-contract">The component contract</a></li></ul></li><li class="chapter open"><span class="arrow">▸</span><a href="#ch3" data-target="ch3">3 · Reconciliation and the Fiber Algorithm</a><ul><li><a href="#ch3-twowhat" data-target="ch3-twowhat">The two things React compares</a></li><li><a href="#ch3-process" data-target="ch3-process">Reconciliation step by step</a></li><li><a href="#ch3-sametype" data-target="ch3-sametype">Same type, different props</a></li><li><a href="#ch3-changetype" data-target="ch3-changetype">Different type, same position</a></li><li><a href="#ch3-hydration" data-target="ch3-hydration">Hydration and the cost of mismatch</a></li><li><a href="#ch3-reconcile-cost" data-target="ch3-reconcile-cost">What reconciliation actually costs</a></li><li><a href="#ch3-concurrent" data-target="ch3-concurrent">Concurrent rendering and interruption</a></li></ul></li><li class="chapter open"><span class="arrow">▸</span><a href="#ch4" data-target="ch4">4 · The Component Lifecycle</a><ul><li><a href="#ch4-phases" data-target="ch4-phases">The three phases</a></li><li><a href="#ch4-render-twice" data-target="ch4-render-twice">Rendering twice, in detail</a></li><li><a href="#ch4-rerender" data-target="ch4-rerender">What causes a re-render</a></li><li><a href="#ch4-commit" data-target="ch4-commit">The commit phase</a></li><li><a href="#ch4-mount-effect" data-target="ch4-mount-effect">Mount, update and cleanup</a></li><li><a href="#ch4-strict-cleanup" data-target="ch4-strict-cleanup">The StrictMode cleanup rehearsal</a></li><li><a href="#ch4-unmount" data-target="ch4-unmount">Unmounting and its traps</a></li></ul></li><li class="chapter open"><span class="arrow">▸</span><a href="#ch5" data-target="ch5">5 · State and the Mental Model</a><ul><li><a href="#ch5-two-kinds" data-target="ch5-two-kinds">Two kinds of state</a></li><li><a href="#ch5-where" data-target="ch5-where">Where should state live?</a></li><li><a href="#ch5-derived" data-target="ch5-derived">Derived state, and why it is not state</a></li><li><a href="#ch5-colocation" data-target="ch5-colocation">Colocating state with its owner</a></li><li><a href="#ch5-lifting" data-target="ch5-lifting">Lifting state up, carefully</a></li><li><a href="#ch5-shape" data-target="ch5-shape">Shape state as a machine</a></li><li><a href="#ch5-immutable" data-target="ch5-immutable">Immutability and why it is required</a></li><li><a href="#ch5-choices" data-target="ch5-choices">Choosing a state library</a></li></ul></li><li class="chapter open"><span class="arrow">▸</span><a href="#ch6" data-target="ch6">6 · useState in Depth</a><ul><li><a href="#ch6-signature" data-target="ch6-signature">The signature and what it returns</a></li><li><a href="#ch6-lazy" data-target="ch6-lazy">Lazy initialisation</a></li><li><a href="#ch6-updater" data-target="ch6-updater">The updater form and stale closures</a></li><li><a href="#ch6-identity" data-target="ch6-identity">State identity is per-position</a></li><li><a href="#ch6-batching" data-target="ch6-batching">Batching and multiple updates in one event</a></li><li><a href="#ch6-objects" data-target="ch6-objects">State as an object, and the spread trap</a></li><li><a href="#ch6-arrays" data-target="ch6-arrays">Arrays and lists without a library</a></li><li><a href="#ch6-custom" data-target="ch6-custom">Writing your own state hook</a></li></ul></li><li class="chapter open"><span class="arrow">▸</span><a href="#ch7" data-target="ch7">7 · useReducer and Complex State Transitions</a><ul><li><a href="#ch7-when" data-target="ch7-when">When to reach for a reducer</a></li><li><a href="#ch7-anatomy" data-target="ch7-anatomy">The anatomy of a reducer</a></li><li><a href="#ch7-actions" data-target="ch7-actions">Designing actions</a></li><li><a href="#ch7-transitions" data-target="ch7-transitions">Transitions that must be atomic</a></li><li><a href="#ch7-side-effects" data-target="ch7-side-effects">Keeping the reducer pure</a></li><li><a href="#ch7-composition" data-target="ch7-composition">Composing reducers</a></li><li><a href="#ch7-testing" data-target="ch7-testing">Testing a reducer</a></li><li><a href="#ch7-redux" data-target="ch7-redux">How this maps to Redux</a></li></ul></li><li class="chapter open"><span class="arrow">▸</span><a href="#ch8" data-target="ch8">8 · Effects and the Rules That Govern Them</a><ul><li><a href="#ch8-what" data-target="ch8-what">What an effect is for</a></li><li><a href="#ch8-dependencies" data-target="ch8-dependencies">The dependency array, precisely</a></li><li><a href="#ch8-cleanup" data-target="ch8-cleanup">Cleanup is not optional</a></li><li><a href="#ch8-classes" data-target="ch8-classes">The four effect categories</a></li><li><a href="#ch8-stale" data-target="ch8-stale">Stale closures and the ref fix</a></li><li><a href="#ch8-abort" data-target="ch8-abort">Cancellation and races</a></li><li><a href="#ch8-traps" data-target="ch8-traps">Seven effect traps</a></li><li><a href="#ch8-custom" data-target="ch8-custom">Abstracting effects into hooks</a></li></ul></li><li class="chapter open"><span class="arrow">▸</span><a href="#ch9" data-target="ch9">9 · Refs, the DOM and Imperative Escape Hatches</a><ul><li><a href="#ch9-useRef" data-target="ch9-useRef">useRef and the two kinds</a></li><li><a href="#ch9-dom" data-target="ch9-dom">Reading and measuring the DOM</a></li><li><a href="#ch9-imperative" data-target="ch9-imperative">Forwarding a handle</a></li><li><a href="#ch9-scroll" data-target="ch9-scroll">Scrolling and viewport</a></li><li><a href="#ch9-focus" data-target="ch9-focus">Focus management</a></li><li><a href="#ch9-avoid" data-target="ch9-avoid">When not to use a ref</a></li><li><a href="#ch9-patterns" data-target="ch9-patterns">Effect plus ref patterns</a></li></ul></li><li class="chapter open"><span class="arrow">▸</span><a href="#ch10" data-target="ch10">10 · Context Without the Sprawl</a><ul><li><a href="#ch10-why" data-target="ch10-why">What context is for</a></li><li><a href="#ch10-default" data-target="ch10-default">Always provide a default value</a></li><li><a href="#ch10-nested" data-target="ch10-nested">The nesting problem</a></li><li><a href="#ch10-split" data-target="ch10-split">Split fast and slow context</a></li><li><a href="#ch10-custom" data-target="ch10-custom">A typed context hook</a></li><li><a href="#ch10-memo" data-target="ch10-memo">Memoising the value</a></li><li><a href="#ch10-selectors" data-target="ch10-selectors">Selector subscriptions</a></li><li><a href="#ch10-vs" data-target="ch10-vs">Context versus a store</a></li></ul></li></ul></nav>
